            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_a71f6a73">B2:443</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Tvende Musiker, hvilke ved den høysalige Kong Christian den Siettes høystbedrøveligste Liigbegængelse, ere blevne holdne</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_9ae4a789">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_5d0750c4">Peder Sparkiær</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_82ee25c8">King Christian VI</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_21_0">
               <date isodate="1746" xml:id="date_3b3579a9">1746</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_21_0">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_21_0">
               <p xml:id="idm115">The cantata, of which the musical sources have not survived, was one of several works that Scheibe composed in connection with the commemoration and funeral of the deceased <persName xml:id="idm116" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christian VI</persName> in 1746. It was performed the first time at the University of Copenhagen on the same day as the funeral took place in Christiansborg Slotskirke, 4 October, to which event Scheibe also composed the music (SchW B2:425). There is no indication as to whom the author of the text might have been, but it is reasonable to assume that it was <persName xml:id="idm117" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peder Sparkiær</persName> with whom Scheibe had previously collaborated. Part of the text corresponds to nos. 1–6 in the cantata performed on the following day in Roskilde (cf. SchW B2:444). It is unlikely that the author of the text was Scheibe; he very seldom wrote Danish texts.</p>
            </history>
